flowchart TB
  accTitle: How an agent evaluates influence
  accDescr: The agent combines position, accepted receipts, information access, relationship state, future narrative value, and identity. A strategic lens organizes that evidence into a contextual estimate of who can move whom and what may happen next. The estimate supports several valid postures and is revised after outcomes.

  Position["Position plus accepted receipts"] --> Lens["Selected strategic lens"]
  Relations["Information access plus relationship state"] --> Lens
  Future["Future value plus competitor identity"] --> Lens

  Lens --> Estimate["Contextual influence estimate"]
  Estimate --> Questions["Who can move whom? Who owes whom? Which story can stick? What changes next?"]

  Questions --> Pressure["Pressure or deal"]
  Questions --> Gather["Gather or repair"]
  Questions --> Restrain["Wait, pass, or stay ambiguous"]

  Pressure --> Outcome["Accepted outcome and new evidence"]
  Gather --> Outcome
  Restrain --> Outcome
  Outcome --> Thread["Reflection updates Strategy Thread"]
  Thread --> Lens

  class Position,Relations,Future inputNode
  class Lens,Estimate,Questions cognitionNode
  class Pressure,Gather,Restrain actionNode
  class Outcome truthNode
  class Thread memoryNode

  classDef inputNode fill:#172554,stroke:#60a5fa,color:#eff6ff,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef cognitionNode fill:#3b0764,stroke:#c084fc,color:#faf5ff,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef actionNode fill:#083344,stroke:#22d3ee,color:#ecfeff,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef truthNode fill:#052e16,stroke:#4ade80,color:#f0fdf4,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef memoryNode fill:#3f2b08,stroke:#facc15,color:#fefce8,stroke-width:1.5px
